<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59796" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρείων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οντος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ruler, lord, master</i>, 
				Ep.
			 word, used in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> mostly of kings and chiefs, esp. of Agamemnon, <i><span class="en">
				1.130
			</span></i>, al. (Com. in parody, of Diomedes, <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				68
			</span></i>); of gods, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπατε
			κρειόντων</span>, of Zeus, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				8.31
			</span></i>, etc.; of Poseidon, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐρὺ κ. ἐνοσίχθων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.751
				</span></i>
			; as an honorary epithet, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ.
			Ἐτεωνεύς</span>, of a squire of Menelaus, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.22
			</span></i>:—so fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρείουσα</span></b>  (once in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρείουσα γυναικῶν</span>, of a
			concubine of Priam, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				22.48
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀντιόπη κ.</span>
			<i>queen</i> Antiope, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				110.6
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Del.</u>
				219
			</span></i>; 
				Dor.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρείοισα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					17.132
				</span></i>
			:—after <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> in the form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρέων</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				8.99
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>N.</u>
				3.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.45
			</span></i>; of Zeus, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				574
			</span></i> (lyr.):—fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρέουσα</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				B.
				3.1
			</span></i>: hence pr. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρέων,
			Κρέουσα</span>. (A participial form (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρείειν γὰρ τὸ ἄρχειν ἔλεγον οἱ
					παλαιοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Artem.
					2.12
				</span></i>
			): <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρείων</span> may be due to
			metrical lengthening or represent <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρήων</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
